<title>UK: Baltic/Black Sea oil exports fall 184 kbpd on week.</title>
<headline>Baltic/Black Sea oil exports fall 184 kbpd on week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil exports from Baltic and Black Sea terminals fell 183,804 barrels per day (bpd) in the last week of March from the previous week to 1.66 million bpd, Petro-Logistics said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The total was 18,874 bpd lower than the same week last year.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based consultancy, tracking tanker movements, said crude exports from Baltic and Black Sea ports fell 67,063 bpd on the week to 911,809 bpd, 150,000 bpd below year-ago levels.</p>
<p>Gas oil exports slumped by 141,035 bpd to 439,693 bpd, which was 47,420 bpd below year-ago levels.</p>
<p>Heavy fuel exports also fell, by 40,003 bpd to 233,893 bpd but were still 99,090 bpd higher than in the same week last year.</p>
<p>The following table provided by Petro-Logistics lists a breakdown in metric tonnes of petroleum exports from the Baltic and Black Sea in the last week of March.</p>
<p>			 Crude	  Fuel    Gas Oil   Mogas/Jet</p>
<p>Total FSU 875,537 252,857 413,412 43,271 1,607,060 Romania/ Bulgaria		 --	   --	   --	  --</p>
<p>TOTAL tonnes	 875,537    252,857   413,412    43,271</p>
<p>1,607,060</p>
<p>TOTAL bpd	    911,809    233,893   439,693    52,543</p>
<p>1,665,574</p>
<p>Change week bpd    -67,063    -40,003  -141,035   +36,661</p>
